{"text": "Okay, so I need to make 24 using the numbers 3, 6, 8, and 13.", "start": 0, "end": 61, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Each number has to be used exactly once, and I can use addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division.", "start": 62, "end": 169, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Hmm, let's see.", "start": 170, "end": 185, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "First, I should recall that 24 can be factored in several ways.", "start": 187, "end": 250, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Like 3 times 8 is 24, or 6 times 4, but I don't have a 4 here.", "start": 251, "end": 313, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Alternatively, 12 times 2, 24 divided by 1, but again, not sure.", "start": 314, "end": 378, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me think step by step.", "start": 379, "end": 405, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me list out the numbers: 3, 6, 8, 13.", "start": 407, "end": 448, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I need to combine them with operations.", "start": 449, "end": 488, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Since 3 and 8 multiply to 24, maybe that's a starting point.", "start": 489, "end": 549, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "If I can get 3 times 8, then maybe use the other numbers to adjust.", "start": 550, "end": 617, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But I have to use all four numbers.", "start": 618, "end": 653, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So if I do 3 * 8 = 24, then I still have 6 and 13 left.", "start": 654, "end": 709, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But I can't just leave them.", "start": 710, "end": 738, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So maybe I need to combine 6 and 13 in some way that cancels them out or adds to the equation.", "start": 739, "end": 833, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Wait, maybe subtract or add them.", "start": 835, "end": 868, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, 13 - 6 = 7.", "start": 869, "end": 893, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 7 + 24 would be 31, which is not helpful.", "start": 894, "end": 940, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Or 13 + 6 = 19, then 24 - 19 = 5.", "start": 941, "end": 974, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not 24.", "start": 975, "end": 982, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Hmm.", "start": 983, "end": 987, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "Alternatively, if I use division.", "start": 988, "end": 1021, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Maybe 13 divided by 6?", "start": 1022, "end": 1044, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "That's about 2.166, which might not be helpful.", "start": 1045, "end": 1092, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Alternatively, maybe start with 6 and 8.", "start": 1094, "end": 1134, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "6 * 8 is 48.", "start": 1135, "end": 1147, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 48 divided by 2 is 24, but I don't have a 2.", "start": 1148, "end": 1197, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But maybe 13 - 3 = 10.", "start": 1198, "end": 1220, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not sure.", "start": 1221, "end": 1230, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "48 minus something?", "start": 1231, "end": 1250, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "48 - (13 + 3) = 48 - 16= 32.", "start": 1251, "end": 1279, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not 24.", "start": 1280, "end": 1287, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Hmm.", "start": 1288, "end": 1292, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "What if I use 13 and 3?", "start": 1294, "end": 1317, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 3 = 10.", "start": 1318, "end": 1330, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 10 multiplied by something.", "start": 1331, "end": 1363, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * 2.4 = 24, but how to get 2.4 from 6 and 8.", "start": 1364, "end": 1411, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "6 divided by 8 is 0.75.", "start": 1412, "end": 1435, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "8 divided by 6 is 1.333.", "start": 1436, "end": 1460, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not helpful.", "start": 1461, "end": 1473, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Alternatively, 8 - 6 = 2.", "start": 1474, "end": 1499, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 10 * 2 = 20.", "start": 1500, "end": 1517, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not 24.", "start": 1518, "end": 1525, "label": "inform"}
